cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software, cite source version 0.9.0 and the exact Git
  commit used to produce your results. This source version has no digital object
  identifier (DOI) or Zenodo record.
type: software
title: "Galadriel's Mirror"
version: 0.9.0
authors:
  - family-names: Mahmoudian
    given-names: Sepehr
repository-code: "https://github.com/sepahead/galadriel"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Galadriel is fail-closed Rust research software for cross-sensor statistical
  consistency monitoring. It uses normalized innovation squared (NIS), cumulative sum
  (CUSUM), and signed common-projection correlation. It also offers an optional
  pairwise mutual-information companion and separate partial information decomposition (PID) studies.
keywords:
  - sensor fusion
  - anomaly detection
  - statistical consistency
  - counter-unmanned aircraft systems
  - information theory
